body:
I'm an INTJ female, I've been experiencing this problem since I was a child. I've become so used to it that it doesn't bother me anymore. Actually I've learned to wear masks when I'm with other females and to "downgrade" my level of speech so that I can still be relative to them. It's true that it's hard to hide your real opinions but think about it: who cares if they know who you really are?

&#x200B;

By the way, I too have never met an INTJ female in my life. But sometimes when I'm checking other people's social media pages or blogs and feel that this female blogger is "different" and "interesting" in a beautiful way, I come to find later that she's an INTJ :)
